  "body": "Found by M3's delta review of PR #1287 (comment 2026-11-12T23:03Z). It was posted after #1287 merged at 23:00Z, so this is on main now.\n\n**What happens.** `install_panic_hook` in `crates/ui/src/win_console.rs` (about lines 135-144) fires at panic time, before any `catch_unwind` runs. The app catches panics on purpose in several places:\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/gpu_init.rs:166` (the GPU probe);\n- `shell.rs:910` and `shell_window.rs:220`;\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs:133` (a STEP kernel panic turns into a clean import error);\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs:155`;\n- `crates/kernel/src/truck_impl.rs`.\n\nSo when the app is started by double-click on Windows, a *handled* panic still pops a modal \"CamCraft stopped unexpectedly\" box. A bad STEP import is one example. The box blocks that thread and uses up the once-per-process flag, so a later real failure shows nothing.\n\nA second, smaller case: if `AttachConsole` succeeds but the `CONOUT$` open fails (around lines 95-97), `CONSOLE_ATTACHED` stays true. Output then goes nowhere, and no box is shown.\n\n**Done means:**\n- the global hook is gone, and on Windows `main` wraps `camcraft_ui::run` in `catch_unwind`, showing the box only for a panic that escapes `run` or a non-zero exit with no console;\n- a failed `CONOUT$` open counts as \"no console\";\n- any pure part (payload to text) has a unit test;\n- the PR's Windows hand-check list includes \"a bad STEP import by double-click shows no box\".\n",
